    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: August 23, 2026</p>

    <h2>Agreement</h2>
    <p>By downloading or using Niyora, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, don't use the app.</p>

    <h2>Eligibility</h2>
    <p>You must be at least 16 years old to use Niyora. By using the app, you confirm that you meet this age requirement.</p>

    <h2>What Niyora Is</h2>
    <p>Niyora is a wellness application that provides guided breathing exercises and mindfulness techniques.</p>

    <h2>Not Medical Advice</h2>
    <p>Niyora is a wellness tool, not a medical device. It does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease or medical condition. The breathing techniques and mindfulness exercises are for general wellness purposes only.</p>
    <p>If you have a respiratory condition, cardiovascular condition, anxiety disorder, or any other health concern, consult your doctor before using breathing exercises. Do not use Niyora as a substitute for professional medical advice.</p>
    <p><strong>Health risks:</strong> Certain breathing techniques may cause dizziness, lightheadedness, hyperventilation, or discomfort. In rare cases, breathing exercises may trigger anxiety or panic in susceptible individuals. If you experience any adverse effects, stop the exercise immediately.</p>

    <h2>Niyora Premium</h2>
    <p>Most of Niyora is free and stays free. The one paid part is the Moon flow, where you tell Moon what happened, reflect on it, regulate, and work out how to respond. You get 5 of those moments free every calendar month, and the count starts again on the first of the next month. Niyora Premium removes that limit. Everything else in the app stays free.</p>
    <p>Premium is an auto-renewing subscription, sold in two plans:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly:</strong> $8.99 per month. No free trial.</li>
      <li><strong>Yearly:</strong> $29.99 per year, with a 7-day free trial if your Apple Account is eligible for one.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Prices are shown here in US dollars. The App Store shows you the price in your own currency before you confirm, and that is the price you pay.</p>
    <p>Payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase. The subscription renews automatically for the same period unless you turn off auto-renew at least 24 hours before the current period ends. Apple charges the renewal to your Apple Account within 24 hours before the period ends.</p>
    <p>If you start the 7-day free trial, it converts into a paid year at the end of the 7 days unless you turn off auto-renew at least 24 hours before it ends. Any unused part of a free trial is forfeited if you buy a subscription before the trial has run out.</p>
    <p><strong>Cancelling:</strong> you cancel through Apple, not through us. On your iPhone, open Settings, tap your name, tap Subscriptions, then turn off auto-renew for Niyora at least 24 hours before the next renewal date. Cancelling stops future charges. Premium keeps working until the end of the period you have already paid for.</p>
    <p><strong>Refunds:</strong> Apple takes the payment and Apple handles refunds. We never see your card or your payment details, and we cannot issue or decline a refund ourselves. Refund requests go to Apple Support.</p>
    <p>If you reinstall Niyora or move to a new iPhone, use "Restore purchase" on the Premium screen to bring an active subscription back on the same Apple Account.</p>
    <p>We may change the price or what Premium includes. A price change never applies to a period you have already paid for. Apple tells you about a price increase before it takes effect, and you can cancel if you do not want to continue at the new price.</p>

